---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why Field Notes exists.">
  <article class="about shell">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About this journal</p>
      <h1>Useful details are worth keeping.</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        Field Notes is a personal record of projects I want to understand—not
        just finish.
      </p>
      <p>
        It begins with a small Intel NUC server: choosing the hardware, making
        services reliable, learning from mistakes, and documenting enough detail
        to make the next rebuild easier.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over time, the same habit will extend to other interests, including
        cycling, race analysis, and whatever else rewards a closer look.
      </p>
      <h2>How posts are written</h2>
      <p>
        Expect commands that can be copied, diagrams that explain the shape of
        a system, and updates when an earlier conclusion turns out to be wrong.
        Posts are Markdown files kept alongside the site, so the archive remains
        portable.
      </p>
      <p><a href={withBase("/posts/")}>Start with the latest notes →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
